    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as the anchor of the offense; his 76.75 efficiency score against Liberatore is our highest on the board, bolstered by a clear platoon advantage and a favorable batting order spot. We are also prioritizing speed-dynamic profiles against softer rotations, evidenced by **Gunnar Henderson** (67.14) and **Jackson Merrill** (63.55) maintaining high marks despite moderate SP opposition. **Andy Pages** remains a high-floor play at 62.47, as his profile gains a specific boost today from a slow opposing delivery, which increases his probability of manufacturing the stolen bases we aggressively weight.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Wade Meckler**, who missed the starting cut with a 35.18 score. While his profile typically provides the category-scarce speed we covet, the combination of facing Misiorowski\u2019s elite 2.07 xERA and a sub-40 efficiency floor necessitated benching him to preserve game caps. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** earns the start at 2B (61.86) because his switch-hitting utility and the favorable 4.93 xERA of the opposing pitcher outweigh the risks associated with his lower spot in the lineup.\n\nWe are monitoring the **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** tandem closely; while both are projected to start, their outcomes are sensitive to the high-variance nature of their respective matchups. Managers should note that **Jordan Westburg** remains unavailable on the IL, and with **Jacob Wilson** currently benched, we are relying on our depth to mitigate the risk of a high-strikeout game from the likes of **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose platoon disadvantage (score 51.38) makes him the most volatile asset in today's outfield rotation.",
